2026-11-06T03:00:21.2169136Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:00:21.2178182Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:00:21.2178648Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:00:21.2179063Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:00:21.2179329Z 
2026-11-06T03:00:21.2179545Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:00:21.2179833Z 
2026-11-06T03:00:21.2180081Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:00:21.2180615Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:00:21.2180882Z 
2026-11-06T03:00:21.2181034Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:00:21.2181381Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:00:21.2181658Z 
2026-11-06T03:00:21.2182042Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:00:21.2182712Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-06T03:00:21.2182921Z 
